@baseUrl = http://localhost:5247
@reportCode = N8v2dBGMZX6wrfaA
@fightId = 106
@sourceId = 7
@playerName = REPLACE_PLAYER

# Application API requests; live loads require WCL credentials and consume quota.
# Replace sample report/fight/player identities with a visible ranking row.
# Both endpoints require an ASCII alphanumeric report code <= 32 chars and fightId > 0.
# edition defaults to retail; supported values are retail, anniversary, mistsofpandaria, era.
# Unlike WorldData/CompRankings, edition aliases and classic_sod are NOT accepted here.
# Player timeline requires sourceId > 0 OR a nonblank playerName; optional specId
# enables specialization-specific corrections. Boss timeline needs no player selection.
# Responses: 200, 400, 403, 404, 429, 502; errors use Problem Details.
# These endpoints have no refresh parameter; explicit loading uses existing WCL cache behavior.
# Incomplete report responses (empty fight metadata, null master data, invalid timing)
# are not cached. Existing invalid cache entries are discarded on read.
# Empty event pages remain cacheable; they do not imply an invalid report.
# Player events include received healing: kind "heal" for direct heals and "hot" for ticks.
# The UI hides both by default; Show healing received enables direct heals and HoT ticks together.
# Received damage uses kind "damage" and its independent Show damage taken toggle.
# Show damage taken also includes recorded mana drains (mana-spent with isManaDrain: true).
# Cast costs are not drains. Drain icons use the incoming lane and amber loss amounts.
# Mana costs/drains use "mana-spent"; effective resource gains use "mana-returned".
# Amount excludes wasted gains. Missing resource costs/passive regeneration are not inferred.
# Show mana received toggles effective gains and is off by default.
# Recorded cast costs appear in muted amber beside the zoom ability name as -250.
# Life Tap casts include effective self mana gains from recorded Life Tap effect 31818
# within 250ms, even with received-mana icons hidden. Zoom shows these in blue.
# Life Tap health percentage drops use the prior snapshot within one second;
# they are explicitly snapshot changes, not inferred absolute damage amounts.
# Mana spent does not have a separate UI toggle or timeline icon.
# Zoom mana event amounts use blue +amount for gains and muted amber -amount for losses.
# Timeline and zoom lines/icon borders share semantic colors: healing casts/received green,
# mana gains blue, mana losses amber, damage received and recorded damaging casts red.
# Resource events share the player's main timeline:
# outgoing casts and self-use resource abilities above; incoming icons below.
# Show received buffs independently toggles lower-lane received buff icons.
# This option does not filter the zoom detail list of active buffs.
# Defensive abilities and health/mana consumables stay above, retaining green/blue colors.
# matching consumable cast/effect icons are not duplicated.
# maxHealth/maxMana are the largest
# recorded capacities for the selected actor during the fight, or null if unavailable.
# Cast timestamp remains completion time. Matched begincast/cast events additionally
# expose castStart and measured duration in milliseconds; unmatched casts have neither.
# Recorded cast/channel intervals keep their time ranges in zoom without Casting/Channeling prefixes.
# Channel durations and interrupted/uncompleted casts are not inferred.
# Completed casts may include castResults, grouped by target and damage/healing.
# Zoom lists each target result on a separate line: +amount to Target for healing.
# Recorded outcomes remain visible while hovering the cast interval, not just completion.
# Hovering a cast icon keeps its detail row visible even outside the measured interval.
# Healing amounts are effective healing; zero results and fully overhealed targets are omitted.
# Zoom also hides values that round to zero at two decimal places.
# Non-periodic effects from the same actor and spell within 250ms after completion qualify.
# Delayed direct damage may match the latest completed same-spell cast up to 3 seconds later,
# requiring the same recorded target, no AoE flag, and no prior damage result for that target.
# Ambiguous simultaneous same-spell casts have no attached results.
# Periodic damage is totaled on the latest completed same-actor, same-spell cast
# with the same recorded target, up to the next cast on that target or fight end.
# Casts on other targets do not steal ticks. Missing target IDs and ambiguous casts
# are not guessed; ticks before the first matching cast are not attributed.
# Periodic healing remains excluded from cast results.
# Missing effects, longer direct-hit delays and different-spell procs are not attributed.
# Timeline master data includes all actor types so NPC/pet targets use recorded names.
# Anniversary NPC 23863 is named Zul'jin rather than the upstream Daakara label.
# Buff uptime requires recorded application and removal events. An unmatched
# application is not extended to fight end; any recorded cast remains visible.
# Report-wide loading retains post-fight buff removals for matching; verified
# intervals extending beyond the selected fight are clipped to its end.
# A post-fight reapplication invalidates an unclosed earlier application so a later
# removal cannot falsely establish continuous in-fight uptime for the new buff.
# Incoming healing, damage and mana events include sourceName when the source
# actor is identified in report master data.
# Event queries request includeResources: true for recorded maxHealth/maxMana.
# Percentage-only health snapshots (maxHitPoints = 100) are not absolute HP;
# maxHealth remains null when the report only supplies those snapshots.
# Heals/HoT ticks and damage expose healthBeforePercent/healthAfterPercent when recorded.
# Zoom health details use signed amount (health after %, signed percentage change, source).
# With absolute HP, before is calculated from post-heal HP minus effective healing.
# With percentage-only HP, before is the previous recorded snapshot, explicitly
# identified by healthBeforeIsPreviousSnapshot (not an exact pre-heal measurement).
# Missing snapshots remain unknown; healing amounts are never subtracted from percentages.
# If absolute maxHealth is missing, estimatedMaxHealth uses effective healing /
# recorded percentage gain. Only gains of at least 10 percentage points qualify
# to limit rounding noise; the median estimate is displayed as Estimated max health.
# Unobserved intervening health changes invalidate the previous snapshot for estimation.
# healthCapacities is a fight-relative series for cursor-specific maximum health.
# Zoom never uses the fight-wide maxHealth/estimatedMaxHealth summary.
# Aura applications/removals/refreshes/stack changes and death invalidate prior capacity
# and pre-heal snapshots conservatively, until new recorded HP or a qualifying heal.
# Each local estimate uses the heal in that interval, not the fight-wide median.
# Percentage-only pre-heal snapshots must be within one second of the heal.
# Known haste/mana/crit-only auras (Bloodlust, Heroism, Moonkin Aura,
# Water Shield, Nature's Swiftness, Elemental Mastery) and armor-only
# Ancestral Fortitude do not invalidate health.
# Unclassified aura changes still invalidate capacity conservatively.
# When hovering just before a hit, zoom may use the next qualifying local estimate
# within one second, only if no intervening capacity boundary occurs.
# Changing this query creates new raw cache keys; old non-resource pages are not reused.

### Replace the sample report code, fight and name with a visible ranking row.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline?fightId={{fightId}}&playerName={{playerName}}&edition=anniversary
Accept: application/json

### Known actor ID instead of a name; optional specId enables Retail specialization corrections.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline?fightId={{fightId}}&sourceId={{sourceId}}&edition=retail&specId=264
Accept: application/json

### All supported player query parameters; select a consistent actor/name pair
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline?fightId={{fightId}}&sourceId={{sourceId}}&playerName={{playerName}}&edition=retail&specId=264
Accept: application/json

### Omitted edition defaults to retail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline?fightId={{fightId}}&sourceId={{sourceId}}
Accept: application/json

### Real enemy casts and observed phase transitions for the reference fight
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline/boss?fightId={{fightId}}&edition=anniversary
Accept: application/json

### Boss timeline with default retail edition
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline/boss?fightId={{fightId}}
Accept: application/json

### Invalid identity is rejected without contacting Warcraft Logs (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/invalid/timeline?fightId=0&edition=anniversary
Accept: application/problem+json

### Missing player selection: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline?fightId={{fightId}}
Accept: application/problem+json

### Aliased edition is rejected for timelines: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/timeline/boss?fightId={{fightId}}&edition=midnight
Accept: application/problem+json

### Replace code with an actual private report to exercise 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/REPLACEPRIVATEREPORT/timeline?fightId=1&playerName={{playerName}}&edition=retail
Accept: application/problem+json

### Replace code with a deleted/nonexistent report to exercise 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/REPLACEMISSINGREPORT/timeline?fightId=1&playerName={{playerName}}&edition=retail
Accept: application/problem+json
